-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Oct 30 19:26:22 UTC 2026 - Martin Hauke <mardnh@gmx.de>

- Update to version 2.9.0
  Added
  * support for transform, style, opacity, and
    preserveAspectRatio="none" on SVG <image> tags.
  * support for colored and uncolored tiling patterns with
    FPDF.create_pattern() and FPDF.use_pattern(), including SVG
    <pattern> elements and pattern fills and strokes on referenced
    <use> shapes.
  * support for unordered lists in multi_cell(markdown=True), using
    *, - or + as bullet markers.
  * documentation on generating rMQR Codes.
  * Python 3.15 is now officially supported.
  * Unicode font detection and enhanced error handling: when text
    cannot be encoded with the current font, the
    FPDFUnicodeEncodingException message now identifies the Unicode
    script (Cyrillic, Arabic, Chinese, etc.) and suggests a suitable
    font available on the system, via the new internal
    UnicodeFontManager.
  Fixed
  * None values in PDF dictionaries are serialized as null instead
    of an invalid Python literal.
  * Homogeneous arrays of PDF string and name objects use their PDF
    serialization, including encryption when applicable.
  * PDF dates pad years below 1000 to four digits.
  * FPDF.set_display_mode() rejects infinite numeric zoom values
    instead of writing invalid PDF numbers.
  * Page-count aliases honor center and right alignment with core
    fonts when text shaping is enabled.
  * 16-bit grayscale images, like 16-bit grayscale PNG files, are
    scaled down to 8 bits instead of being converted to RGBA, which
    made every value above 255 white, and keep the transparency of
    their tRNS color key.
  * Tables inside FPDF.unbreakable() are replayed with their rows
    and cells intact when the block is moved to a new page.
  * FPDF.table() raises a clear ValueError naming the column when
    text_align is a tuple with fewer values than the table has
    columns, like it does for col_widths, instead of an IndexError.
  * FPDF.table(): a cell with a colspan below 1 spans one column,
    like a rowspan below 1 already spans one row, instead of raising
    ZeroDivisionError or FPDFException or breaking the column layout
  * Synchronize font_style and emphasis setters with font selection
    and state tracking - cf. issue #1223.
  * FPDF.table() raises ValueError: ... is not a valid
    TableBordersLayout for an unknown borders_layout name, like it
    does for cell_fill_mode and v_align, instead of a bare
    AttributeError.
  * FPDF.set_font() and FPDF.add_font() treat a repeated style
    letter as the same style: style="BB" is bold, instead of raising
    FPDFException: Undefined font: helveticaBB.
  * Document outlines count all visible descendants and link
    siblings by parent, retaining bookmarks when the hierarchy
    starts below the top level.
  * Annotation colors and border widths are serialized as PDF
    numbers without exponent notation.
  * Checksums for compressed embedded files are calculated from the
    original file bytes, as required by the PDF specification.
  * Repeated annotation flags no longer change unrelated flag bits;
    annotation flags are combined with bitwise OR.
  * FPDF.ink_annotation() raises a clear ValueError for an empty
    coords sequence, instead of ValueError: min() iterable argument
    is empty.
  * SVG images with a zero width or height disable rendering instead
    of using viewport dimensions.
  * FPDF.write_html() uses the first available font of a <font face>
    list, like browsers, as in face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif",
    with the generic serif, sans-serif and monospace families
    rendered by the core fonts, instead of raising FPDFException:
    Undefined font.
  * SVG gradient stop-opacity accepts percentages, clamps
    out-of-range values to 0-1, and combines with the color's alpha
    channel instead of replacing it.
  * SVG basic-shape coordinates and corner radii now accept absolute
    length units.
  * SVG transforms accept numbers written in scientific notation,
    such as scale(1e-3), instead of silently ignoring the transform.
  * SVG gradient stops honor inline style declarations of
    stop-opacity over the corresponding presentation attribute.
  * SVG length and angle attributes accept scientific notation, such
    as width="1e2pt", instead of raising ValueError.
  * Floating-point numbers in PDF arrays, dictionaries and
    destinations are written without exponent notation, preserving
    their values and allowing very small numeric zoom factors to be
    read correctly.
  * SVG byte strings and BytesIO inputs accept a UTF-8 BOM and XML
    whitespace after <svg or <?xml, instead of being sent to the
    raster image loader.
  * SVG import: a <polygon> or <polyline> whose points has an error
    (an invalid coordinate or an odd number of them) is drawn up to
    the last complete point before it, and one with empty points
    draws nothing, as the SVG specification says, instead of
    raising IndexError.
  * FPDF.write_html() ignores an unsupported align value on <td>,
    <th> and <tr>, such as middle, like it already does for <p>,
    instead of raising ValueError.
  * FPDF.regular_polygon() raises ValueError: 'numSides' parameter
    must be equal or greater than 1 for numSides below 1, instead of
    silently writing a path with no points (a bare h S, which closes
    a path that was never started).
  * Bulleted text-column paragraphs now honor their top margins,
    indented paragraphs retain the column's right boundary, and HTML
    list items honor their TextStyle.t_margin - based on PR #1218.
  * FPDF.text_columns() raises a clear ValueError for ncols below
    1, like insert_toc_placeholder() does for pages, instead of a
    ZeroDivisionError or an unrelated Not enough horizontal space
    error when rendering.
  * FPDF() and FPDF.add_page() raise FPDFPageFormatException: Width
    and height must be positive numbers for a page format whose
    width or height is zero or negative, such as (0, 0), instead of
    writing a page with an empty or inverted /MediaBox.
  * FPDF.write_html() now supports CSS length units (px, pt) and
    surrounding whitespace in dimension attributes for <table>,
    <td>, <th>, <hr>, and <img> elements without raising ValueError.
  * FPDF.write_html() reads a CSS font-size on <font> with its unit,
    like browsers, as in style="font-size: 14pt" or "12px", instead
    of silently ignoring it; a number without a unit is still in
    points.
  * FPDF.write_html() supports <ul type="square">, the third
    standard HTML bullet type, instead of raising
    NotImplementedError: Unicode fonts use ▪ and core fonts fall
    back to the bullet.
  * FPDF.write_html() accepts the <ul type> keywords in any case,
    like browsers: <ul type="CIRCLE"> and <ul type="Square"> no
    longer raise NotImplementedError.
  * FPDF.write_html() supports <ul type="none">, rendering the list
    items without a marker like browsers do, instead of raising
    NotImplementedError.
  * FPDF.write_html() keeps the default bullet for an empty or
    unknown <ul type>, such as type="" or a misspelled type="disk",
    like browsers and like <ol> already does, instead of raising
    NotImplementedError.
  * SVG import: color keywords are case-insensitive (fill="RED"),
    and fill / stroke accept transparent, painting nothing like
    none, instead of raising ValueError
  * FPDF.write_html() accepts css rgb(R, G, B) colors, and colors
    with surrounding spaces, in color and bgcolor attributes
    instead of raising ValueError.
  * FPDF.write_html() accepts a legacy HTML color of six hex
    digits without the leading #, like browsers do, as in
    bgcolor="eeeeee" or <font color="ff0000">, instead of raising
    ValueError.
  * FPDF.write_html() ignores color="transparent" and
    bgcolor="transparent" like browsers, keeping the inherited text
    or background color, instead of raising ValueError.
  * FPDF.write_html() ignores an invalid CSS color on a heading,
    like browsers, as in <h1 style="color: nope">, keeping the color
    attribute or the heading's default color, instead of raising
    ValueError.
  * FPDF.write_html() no longer raises IndexError on an
    <ol type="a"> or <ol type="A"> list with more than 26 items:
    like browsers, letters continue with aa, ab... and a start
    below 1 shows as a number.
  * FPDF.write_html() numbers an <ol> with an unknown type, such as
    type="disc", as 1, 2, 3, like browsers, instead of raising
    NotImplementedError.
  * FPDF.write_html() supports <li value="N"> in ordered lists:
    like browsers, the item is numbered N and the following ones
    continue from it.
  * FPDF.write_html() no longer raises KeyError: 'href' on an <a>
    element without an href attribute, such as a named anchor (<a
    name="intro">); its text is rendered as plain text.
  * FPDF.set_display_mode() raises FPDFException: Incorrect zoom
    display mode for a negative or non-numeric zoom, such as -50
    or None, like it does for an unknown zoom name, instead of
    writing an invalid /OpenAction zoom or failing later in
    output().
  * FPDF.write_html() no longer warns about a missing end tag for
    the HTML void elements <meta>, <link>, <col>, <wbr>, <input>,
    <base>, <area>, <embed>, <source> and <track>, which never
    have one, as in the <head> of an HTML email.
  * FPDF.write_html() treats an invalid colspan or rowspan on <td>
    / <th>, or one below 1, as 1 like browsers do, instead of
    raising ValueError or ZeroDivisionError.
  * FPDF.write_html() stops a rowspan that goes past the last row
    of a <table> at the last row, like browsers, instead of
    raising FPDFException: Rowspan extends beyond end of table.
  * FPDF.write_html() renders a <table> whose width is wider than
    the page, such as width="150%", at the page width with a
    warning, and ignores a negative width like browsers, instead
    of raising ValueError.
  * FPDF.write_html() no longer raises ValueError: Invalid
    .col_widths specified on a table whose first row gives a width
    to only some of its cells, such as
    <td width="50%">a</td><td>b</td>: like browsers, the other
    cells share the remaining space, after the gaps of cellspacing;
    a cell with a colspan gives each column it spans an equal part
    of its width.
  * warning detection during FPDFRecorder.replay() now correctly
    identifies context managers (contextlib.AbstractContextManager,
    @contextmanager, custom context managers) within unbreakable()
    sections.
  * SVG import: opacity, fill-opacity and stroke-opacity accept
    percentages (50%), and an out-of-range opacity is clamped to
    0-1 like the other two instead of raising ValueError.
  * css rgb() colors accept percentages, as in rgb(100%, 0%, 50%)
    (clamped to 0%-100%), in SVG import and FPDF.write_html()
    instead of raising ValueError.
  * hex color strings, such as in set_fill_color("#..."), must
    contain only hexadecimal digits: "#1 2345" and "#+12345" were
    silently read as #012345, and "#xyz" raised an unclear invalid
    literal for int() error; all now raise ValueError: ... could
    not be interpreted as a RGB(A) hex string.
  * FPDF.ink_annotation() computes the horizontal position of the
    annotation rectangle (/Rect) from the x coordinates of the path
    instead of the y coordinates, so the rectangle encloses the
    drawn path; it could previously lie outside the page.
  * FPDF.set_auto_page_break() and FPDF.set_margin() raise
    ValueError: Bottom margin must be zero or a positive number for
    a negative margin, instead of placing the page break below the
    bottom edge of the page, so that the last lines before each
    break were written off the page and lost.
  * FPDF.embed_file() accepts empty byte content and rejects
    simultaneous path and byte sources even when the bytes are
    empty.
  * FPDF.set_line_width() raises ValueError: Line width must be
    zero or a positive number for a negative width, like
    set_dash_pattern() does for a negative dash length, instead of
    writing a negative line width that the PDF specification does
    not allow.
  * FPDF.star() raises ValueError: 'corners' parameter must be
    equal or greater than 1 for corners below 1, instead of a bare
    ZeroDivisionError for corners=0 and silently drawing nothing
    for a negative value.
  * set_text_color(), set_fill_color() and set_draw_color() report
    a component outside 0-255 as given: set_text_color(300) now
    raises ValueError: color component 300 not in range [0, 255]
    instead of 1.1764705882352942 not in range [0.0, 1.0].
  * An internal link with an index that FPDF.add_link() did not
    return now raises a clear ValueError, like a link without a
    page number, instead of a bare AssertionError (or a KeyError
    with python -O).
  * FPDF.write_html() no longer writes the content of <style> and
    <script> elements into the document as text, like browsers, so
    an HTML page or email with a <style> block no longer shows its
    CSS.
  * FPDF.add_page() and FPDF.set_page_label() raise ValueError:
    'label_start' parameter must be equal or greater than 1 for a
    label_start below 1, instead of writing an invalid /St value
    that the PDF specification requires to be 1 or greater.
  * FPDF.set_stretching() raises ValueError: Stretching must be a
    positive number for a stretching of zero or below, instead of
    laying out text with no width: justified text was all put on a
    single line, and other text raised an unrelated Not enough
    horizontal space to render a single character error.
  * FPDF.write_html() raises NotImplementedError: Unsupported
    nested HTML tags inside <td> element: <table> for a <table>
    nested in a table cell, like for the other unsupported nested
    tags, instead of a bare AssertionError with no message.
  Changed
  * Updated the Portuguese tutorial, including tutorials 4 and 5
    and the new PDF/A tutorial 7 - cf. PR #2038.
  * Modernized type annotations for Python 3.11+, using union
    syntax, standard collection types, and typing.Self
  * Removed redundant trailing zeros from numbers in PDF
    dictionaries and arrays outside content streams, preserving
    existing numeric precision.
  Removed
  * Removed the defusedxml dependency: SVG parsing now relies on
    the standard-library ElementTree parser and Expat amplification
    limits; bounded internal entities are accepted, cf. issue #1793
  * support for Python 3.10, that reached end-of-life.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Oct 12 13:21:51 UTC 2026 - Martin Hauke <mardnh@gmx.de>

- Update to version 2.8.9
  Added
  * align parameter for FPDF.alias_nb_pages() to control horizontal
    alignment (Align.L, Align.C, Align.R) of substitution text
    inside reserved alias space.
  * support for page number alias substitution with bidirectional
    / RTL text shaping.
  * appearance parameter for FPDF.file_attachment_annotation(),
    accepting FileAttachmentAppearance.HIDDEN to give the
    annotation an empty appearance stream so its default icon is
    not displayed while the file stays embedded and reachable.
  * Turkish translation of the Tuto 7 - Creating PDF/A Documents
    tutorial section, along with fixes for duplicated clauses and
    mistranslations in the Tuto 2, 4 & 6 descriptions.
  Fixed
  * escaped Markdown markers adjacent to emphasis markers in link
    labels no longer lose literal characters or apply unintended
    styling.
  * PDF serialization of boolean and null values: booleans in
    arrays and dictionaries now use lowercase true and false,
    including in mixed numeric/boolean arrays; None in arrays is
    serialized as null; and filtering empty dictionary fields
    preserves False and numeric zero values.
  * SVG percentage width and height values with surrounding
    whitespace (e.g. width="100% ") no longer raise ValueError.
  * PDF/A-1 documents using TrueType or CFF-based CID fonts now
    include a /CIDSet stream in each font descriptor, as required
    by ISO 19005-1 (veraPDF rule 6.3.5-3).
  * split font /ToUnicode and /Encoding CMap mappings into blocks
    of at most 100 entries, as required by the PDF specification.
  * visual gap in rendering subsequent text after {nb} page alias
    when text shaping is enabled.
  * FPDF.write_html() no longer raises IndexError: pop from empty
    list when a <ul> or <ol> element carries a line-height that
    is not a bare number (e.g. line-height: normal or line-height:
    1.5em); such values are now ignored, and the default line
    height is used, consistently with <p line-height="x">.
  * FPDF.write_html() now renders list bullets with correct font
    styling instead of inheriting preceding heading (e.g. <h1>)
    styles.
  * table cells landing in the wrong column when a row was covered
    by several rowspans that did not start in column order.
  * Padding.new() now accepts 1-element sequences per CSS shorthand
    rules and preserves existing Padding instances without
    redundant allocations.
- Update to version 2.8.8
  Added
  * Punjabi (pa) tutorial translation.
  * FPDF.svg_limits and SVGLimits to configure SVG complexity
    limits while rendering SVG images.
  * resource_access_policy and Security considerations documentation
  * FPDF.optional_content() context manager to mark content as
    visible on screen only or in print only, using PDF Optional
    Content Groups.
  * basic support for SVG <symbol> elements in the SVG parser.
  * basic support for SVG <switch> elements in the SVG parser.
  * support for keeping aspect ratio for images in templates.
  Fixed
  * Addresses CVE-2026-114609 (bsc#1287182), CVE-2026-114610 (bsc#1287183)
  * custom height passed to Paragraph.ln() in a text region is now
    applied to the line it terminates instead of the first line of
    the following paragraph.
  * the optional numpy import in image_parsing.py no longer crashes
    on CPUs unsupported by numpy's manylinux wheel baseline;
    RuntimeError is now treated the same as ImportError, so numpy
    degrades to unavailable instead of taking down import fpdf.
  * font state (family, style, size, current font, and the
    page-level "font is set" flag) no longer leaks back onto the
    FPDF instance after a text_columns() / text_region() context
    exits, so a subsequent pdf.cell() / pdf.write() renders at the
    caller's font instead of the last paragraph's.
  * text rendering when the first text on a page starts with a
    fallback glyph.
  * preserve boundary-neutral formatting during bidirectional text
    preprocessing.
  * transform application on user space gradients.
  * dependency extras for camelot-py and endesive on pyproject.toml
  * preserve link annotations during dry-run of FPDF.multi_cell.
  * preserve two consecutive markdown links (without space
    inbetween).
  * support markdown style around markdown links.
  * Reset gstate for ToC-rendering.
  * preserve markdown format in FPDF.multi_cell in dry-run.
  * fix page order after dry-run of FPDF.multi_cell in ToC.
  * rendering SVG arcs with very small sweeps that previously
    rounded to zero.
  * spurious "Not enough horizontal space to render a single
    character" error when text without break opportunities is
    split into many small fragments, e.g. by a fallback font
    alternating with the main fon
  * number of surviving escape characters.
  * leading spaces on new lines inside <pre> and <pre><code> blocks
    are no longer dropped.
  * FPDF.set_font() can restore current_font when the selected font
    state diverged.
  * embed CID-keyed CFF fonts as raw CFF programs so browser PDF
    viewers render them correctly.
  * fixed broken links on documentation not directly leading to the
    API reference.
  * reject SVG <use> cycles and excessive nested expansion to
    prevent resource exhaustion in FPDF.image().
  * count SVG <switch> elements in SVG complexity limits.
  * declare the default base state and display order for Optional
    Content Groups so PDF viewers can list layers correctly.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Apr 11 16:39:15 UTC 2026 - Dirk Müller <dmueller@suse.com>

- update to 2.8.7:
  * types on `FPDF.title`, `FPDF.add_font()` and `FPDF.output()`
  * added missing files to navigation tree in mkdocs.yml - thanks
    to @paulsuh
  * reverted changes to `ImageInfo` that impacted user-facing API
  * prefer outline glyphs over bitmap if the font has both
- update to 2.8.6:
  * support for `FPDF.transform()` context manager to apply
    geometric transformations (translation, rotation, scaling,
    skewing) to the current graphics state
  * support for SVG `` and `` elements - _cf._ issue #1580 -
  * mypy and pyright checks in the CI pipeline to enforce strict
    typing
  * support WOFF and WOFF2 fonts
  * TTC/OTC face selection via `collection_font_number` in
    `add_font()`
  * CID-keyed CFF font embedding support
  * Microsoft Symbol font remapping for non-Unicode cmaps
  * support for EBDT/EBLC bitmap fonts
  * the `A5` value that could be specified as page `format` to
    the `FPDF` constructor was slightly incorrect, and the
    corresponding page dimensions have been fixed. This could
    lead to a minor change in your documents dimensions if you
    used this `A5` page format. - _cf._ issue #1699
  * a bug when rendering empty tables with `INTERNAL` layout,
    that caused an extra border to be rendered due to an
    erroneous use of `list.index()` - _cf._ issue #1669
  * edge cases where tiny floating-point drift could trigger
    incorrect behaviour like issue #1393
  * parentheses are now escaped in more places. This fixes
    embedding a file with a single parenthesis in the filename,
    but might also have impacts on e.g. section names.
  * parsing markdown sequences with escape character - _cf._
    issue #1236 - thanks @amidou-naba
  * improved performance when rendering paths, SVGs, and opaque
    raster images with an alpha channel - _cf._ PR #1675
  * typing annotations added across the codebase as part of the
    strict typing rollout
  * graphics state snapshots now use a `GraphicsState` dataclass
    dataclass for clearer usage and stronger typing
  * `rotation()`, `skew()`, and `mirror()` now delegate to
    `transform()` for standardized transform application
  * ImageInfo now uses typed dictionaries for clearer usage and
    stronger typing

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Jan 19 15:16:04 UTC 2026 - Markéta Machová <mmachova@suse.com>

- Update to 2.8.5
  * added tutorial "tuto7" (in English and German) with documentation to create PDF/A files with fpdf2
  * support for many different text/paragraph formatings added
  * improved SVG image parsing speed by 50% to 70%
  * Python 3.14 is now officially supported
  * changed libtiff detection logic to maintain compatibility with pillow v12
  * many more bug fixes and improvements, see upstream CHANGELOG.md

